---
id: environment-variables
title: Environment Variables
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn how to securely configure and use environment variables in your TanStack Start application across different contexts (server functions, client code, and build processes)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read env per-request, not at module scope."}]},{"type":"text","value":" On Cloudflare Workers and other edge SSR runtimes, env vars are injected at request time — module-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env.X"},{"type":"text","value":" reads run before the env exists and evaluate to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" even on the server. Always read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".handler()"},{"type":"text","value":", middleware "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".server()"},{"type":"text","value":", server-route handlers, or other per-request callbacks. Reading at module scope also risks inlining secrets into the client bundle. (On Cloudflare Workers specifically, the canonical way to read env from anywhere — including module scope — is the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/environment-variables/","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloudflare:workers"},{"type":"text","value":" env binding"}]},{"type":"text","value":".)"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start automatically loads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files and makes variables available in both server and client contexts with proper security boundaries. Server code can read unprefixed variables from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":"; client code can only read variables exposed by your build tool's public prefix."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"mixed"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"# .env\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb\nVITE_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"// Server function - can access any environment variable\nconst getUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const db = await connect(process.env.DATABASE_URL) // ✅ Server-only\n  return db.user.findFirst()\n})\n\n// Client component - only VITE_ prefixed variables\nexport function AppHeader() {\n  return <h1>{import.meta.env.VITE_APP_NAME}</h1> // ✅ Client-safe\n}","lang":"typescript"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"mixed"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"# .env\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"// Server function - can access any environment variable\nconst getUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const db = await connect(process.env.DATABASE_URL) // ✅ Server-only\n  return db.user.findFirst()\n})\n\n// Client component - only PUBLIC_ prefixed variables by default\nexport function AppHeader() {\n  return <h1>{import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APP_NAME}</h1> // ✅ Client-safe\n}","lang":"typescript"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variable-contexts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable Contexts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"server-side-context-server-functions-api-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-Side Context (Server Functions & API Routes)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server functions can access "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"any"}]},{"type":"text","value":" environment variable using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\n// Database connection (server-only)\nconst connectToDatabase = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const connectionString = process.env.DATABASE_URL // No prefix needed\n  const apiKey = process.env.EXTERNAL_API_SECRET // Stays on server\n\n  // These variables are never exposed to the client\n  return await database.connect(connectionString)\n})\n\n// Authentication (server-only)\nconst authenticateUser = createServerFn()\n  .validator(z.object({ token: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const jwtSecret = process.env.JWT_SECRET // Server-only\n    return jwt.verify(data.token, jwtSecret)\n  })","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"client-side-context-components-client-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-Side Context (Components & Client Code)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client code can only access variables with your build tool's public prefix."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"mixed"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite exposes variables with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Client configuration\nexport function ApiProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL     // ✅ Public\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_KEY  // ✅ Public\n\n  // This would be undefined (security feature):\n  // const secret = import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL   // ❌ Undefined\n\n  return (\n    <ApiContext.Provider value={{ apiUrl, apiKey }}>\n      {children}\n    </ApiContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\n// Feature flags\nexport function FeatureGatedComponent() {\n  const enableNewFeature = import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_FEATURE === 'true'\n\n  if (!enableNewFeature) return null\n\n  return <NewFeature />\n}","lang":"typescript"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"mixed"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rsbuild exposes variables with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix by default:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Client configuration\nexport function ApiProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL // ✅ Public\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_KEY // ✅ Public\n\n  // This would be undefined (security feature):\n  // const secret = import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL // ❌ Undefined\n\n  return (\n    <ApiContext.Provider value={{ apiUrl, apiKey }}>\n      {children}\n    </ApiContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\n// Feature flags\nexport function FeatureGatedComponent() {\n  const enableNewFeature = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ENABLE_NEW_FEATURE === 'true'\n\n  if (!enableNewFeature) return null\n\n  return <NewFeature />\n}","lang":"typescript"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-file-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment File Setup"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"file-hierarchy-loaded-in-order","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File Hierarchy (Loaded in Order)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start automatically loads environment files in this order:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".env.local          # Local overrides (add to .gitignore)\n.env.production     # Production-specific variables\n.env.development    # Development-specific variables\n.env                # Default variables (commit to git)"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"example-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":".env"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (committed to repository):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Public configuration (Vite uses VITE_; Rsbuild uses PUBLIC_ by default)\nVITE_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\n\n# Server configuration templates\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/myapp_dev\nREDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":".env.local"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (add to .gitignore):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Override for local development\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/myapp_local\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\nJWT_SECRET=your-local-secret","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":".env.production"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Production overrides\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.myapp.com\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.myapp.com\nDATABASE_POOL_SIZE=20","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"database-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Database Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/lib/database.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst getDatabaseConnection = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const config = {\n    url: process.env.DATABASE_URL,\n    maxConnections: parseInt(process.env.DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS || '10'),\n    ssl: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',\n  }\n\n  return createConnection(config)\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"authentication-provider-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication Provider Setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/lib/auth.ts (Server)\nexport const authConfig = {\n  secret: process.env.AUTH_SECRET,\n  providers: {\n    auth0: {\n      domain: process.env.AUTH0_DOMAIN,\n      clientId: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n      clientSecret: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET, // Server-only\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// src/components/AuthProvider.tsx (Client)\nexport function AuthProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <Auth0Provider\n      domain={import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN}\n      clientId={import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID}\n      // No client secret here - it stays on the server\n    >\n      {children}\n    </Auth0Provider>\n  )\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"external-api-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External API Integration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/lib/external-api.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\n// Server-side API calls (can use secret keys)\nconst fetchUserData = createServerFn()\n  .validator(z.object({ userId: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(\n      `${process.env.EXTERNAL_API_URL}/users/${data.userId}`,\n      {\n        headers: {\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.EXTERNAL_API_SECRET}`,\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n        },\n      },\n    )\n\n    return response.json()\n  })\n\n// Client-side API calls (public endpoints only)\nexport function usePublicData() {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL\n\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['public-data'],\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`${apiUrl}/public/stats`).then((r) => r.json()),\n  })\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"feature-flags-and-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature Flags and Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/config/features.ts\nexport const featureFlags = {\n  enableNewDashboard: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD === 'true',\n  enableAnalytics: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS === 'true',\n  debugMode: import.meta.env.VITE_DEBUG_MODE === 'true',\n}\n\n// Usage in components\nexport function Dashboard() {\n  if (featureFlags.enableNewDashboard) {\n    return <NewDashboard />\n  }\n\n  return <LegacyDashboard />\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"typescript-declarations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Declarations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/env.d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" to add type safety:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // Client-side environment variables\n  readonly VITE_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly VITE_API_URL: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n  readonly VITE_SENTRY_DSN?: string\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD?: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n\n// Server-side environment variables\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      readonly DATABASE_URL: string\n      readonly REDIS_URL: string\n      readonly JWT_SECRET: string\n      readonly AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET: string\n      readonly STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: string\n      readonly NODE_ENV: 'development' | 'production' | 'test'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {}","lang":"typescript"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"/// <reference types=\"@rsbuild/core/types\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // Client-side environment variables\n  readonly PUBLIC_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_API_URL: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN?: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD?: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n\n// Server-side environment variables\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      readonly DATABASE_URL: string\n      readonly REDIS_URL: string\n      readonly JWT_SECRET: string\n      readonly AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET: string\n      readonly STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: string\n      readonly NODE_ENV: 'development' | 'production' | 'test'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {}","lang":"typescript"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runtime-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Zod for runtime validation of environment variables:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/config/env.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  DATABASE_URL: z.url(),\n  JWT_SECRET: z.string().min(32),\n  NODE_ENV: z.enum(['development', 'production', 'test']),\n})\n\nconst clientEnvSchema = z.object({\n  VITE_APP_NAME: z.string(),\n  VITE_API_URL: z.url(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: z.string(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: z.string(),\n})\n\n// Validate server environment\n// NOTE: Module-level parse runs at module load. Fine for Node.js;\n// on Cloudflare Workers (and other edge runtimes) `process.env` is\n// empty at module load, so wrap this in a function and call it\n// inside `.handler()` instead:\n//\n//   export const getServerEnv = () => envSchema.parse(process.env)\n//\n// Then read `getServerEnv()` per-request from server functions/middleware.\nexport const serverEnv = envSchema.parse(process.env)\n\n// Validate client environment (build-time, always safe)\nexport const clientEnv = clientEnvSchema.parse(import.meta.env)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"security-best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security Best Practices"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-never-expose-secrets-to-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Never Expose Secrets to Client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ WRONG - Secret exposed to client bundle\nconst config = {\n  apiKey: import.meta.env.VITE_SECRET_API_KEY, // This will be in your JS bundle!\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Keep secrets on server\nconst getApiData = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\n    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.SECRET_API_KEY}` },\n  })\n  return response.json()\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-use-appropriate-prefixes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Use Appropriate Prefixes"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# ✅ Server-only (no prefix)\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://...\nJWT_SECRET=super-secret-key\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...\n\n# ✅ Client-safe (Vite uses VITE_; Rsbuild uses PUBLIC_ by default)\nVITE_APP_NAME=My App\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My App\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-validate-required-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Validate Required Variables"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/config/validation.ts\nconst requiredServerEnv = ['DATABASE_URL', 'JWT_SECRET'] as const\n\nconst requiredClientEnv = ['VITE_APP_NAME', 'VITE_API_URL'] as const // Use PUBLIC_ names for Rsbuild\n\n// Validate on server startup\nfor (const key of requiredServerEnv) {\n  if (!process.env[key]) {\n    throw new Error(`Missing required environment variable: ${key}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// Validate client environment at build time\nfor (const key of requiredClientEnv) {\n  if (!import.meta.env[key]) {\n    throw new Error(`Missing required environment variable: ${key}`)\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All sensitive variables are server-only (no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client variables use your build tool's public prefix ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" for Vite, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" for Rsbuild)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env.local"},{"type":"text","value":" is in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gitignore"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production environment variables are configured on hosting platform"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required environment variables are validated at startup"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No hardcoded secrets in source code"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Database URLs use connection pooling in production"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API keys are rotated regularly"}]}],"checked":false}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-problems","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Problems"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variable-is-undefined","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable is Undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env.MY_VARIABLE"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add correct prefix"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use your build tool's public prefix (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_MY_VARIABLE"},{"type":"text","value":" for Vite or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_MY_VARIABLE"},{"type":"text","value":" for Rsbuild)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restart development server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" after adding new variables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check file location"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file must be in project root"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify build tool configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Ensure variables are properly injected"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# ❌ Won't work in client code\nAPI_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works in client code\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ❌ Won't bundle the variable (assuming it is not set in the environment of the build)\nnpm run build\n\n# ✅ Works in client code and will bundle the variable for production\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runtime-client-environment-variables-in-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime Client Environment Variables in Production"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": If public client variables are replaced at bundle time only, how to make runtime variables available on the client?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass variables from the server down to the client:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const getRuntimeVar = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(() => {\n  return process.env.MY_RUNTIME_VAR // notice `process.env` on the server, and no public prefix\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const foo = await getRuntimeVar()\n    return { foo }\n  },\n  component: RouteComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  const { foo } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  // ... use your variable however you want\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"variable-not-updating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable Not Updating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Environment variable changes aren't reflected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restart development server"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check if you're modifying the correct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify file hierarchy ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env.local"},{"type":"text","value":" overrides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"typescript-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Property 'VITE_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Property 'PUBLIC_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Add to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/env.d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ImportMetaEnv {\n  readonly VITE_MY_VAR: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_MY_VAR: string\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"security-secret-exposed-to-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security: Secret Exposed to Client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Sensitive data appearing in client bundle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix from sensitive variables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move sensitive operations to server functions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use build tools to verify no secrets in client bundle"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"build-errors-in-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build Errors in Production"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Missing environment variables in production build"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure variables on hosting platform"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate required variables at build time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use deployment-specific "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-build-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Build Configuration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"static-node-env-replacement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" Replacement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, TanStack Start statically replaces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env.NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server builds"}]},{"type":"text","value":" at build time. This enables dead code elimination (tree-shaking) for development-only code paths in your server bundle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why this matters:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Vite automatically replaces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env.NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" in client builds, but server builds run in Node.js where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" is a real runtime object. Without static replacement, code like this would remain in your production server bundle:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {\n  // This code would NOT be eliminated without static replacement\n  enableDevTools()\n  logDebugInfo()\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With static replacement enabled (the default), the build tool sees "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"production\" === 'development'"},{"type":"text","value":" and eliminates the entire block."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"configuring-static-replacement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuring Static Replacement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The replacement is controlled by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server.build.staticNodeEnv"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport viteReact from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      server: {\n        build: {\n          // Replace process.env.NODE_ENV at build time (default: true)\n          staticNodeEnv: true,\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n    viteReact(),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      server: {\n        build: {\n          // Replace process.env.NODE_ENV at build time (default: true)\n          staticNodeEnv: true,\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title":"rsbuild.config.ts","file":"rsbuild.config.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The replacement value is determined in this order:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env.NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" at build time (if set)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The build tool's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode"},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g., from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--mode staging"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"production\""},{"type":"text","value":" (fallback)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"when-to-disable-static-replacement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to Disable Static Replacement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staticNodeEnv: false"},{"type":"text","value":" if you need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" to remain dynamic at runtime:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"tanstackStart({\n  server: {\n    build: {\n      staticNodeEnv: false, // Keep NODE_ENV dynamic at runtime\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common reasons to disable:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same build, multiple environments"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Deploying one build artifact to staging and production"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime environment detection"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Code that must check the actual runtime environment"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Testing production builds locally"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Running production builds with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NODE_ENV=development"}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Disabling static replacement means development-only code paths will remain in your production bundle and be evaluated at runtime."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" If you disable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staticNodeEnv"},{"type":"text","value":", you "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"must"}]},{"type":"text","value":" set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NODE_ENV=production"},{"type":"text","value":" at runtime when running your server in production. Without this, React (and possibly other libraries) will run in development mode, which is significantly slower and includes extra warnings and checks not intended for production use."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./code-execution-patterns.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Execution Patterns"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about server vs client code execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-functions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn more about server-side code"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./hosting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Platform-specific environment variable configuration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official Vite documentation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://rsbuild.dev/guide/advanced/env-vars","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rsbuild Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official Rsbuild documentation"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"environment-variable-contexts","text":"Environment Variable Contexts","level":2},{"id":"server-side-context-server-functions-api-routes","text":"Server-Side Context (Server Functions & API Routes)","level":3},{"id":"client-side-context-components-client-code","text":"Client-Side Context (Components & Client Code)","level":3},{"id":"environment-file-setup","text":"Environment File Setup","level":2},{"id":"file-hierarchy-loaded-in-order","text":"File Hierarchy (Loaded in Order)","level":3},{"id":"example-setup","text":"Example Setup","level":3},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common Patterns","level":2},{"id":"database-configuration","text":"Database Configuration","level":3},{"id":"authentication-provider-setup","text":"Authentication Provider Setup","level":3},{"id":"external-api-integration","text":"External API Integration","level":3},{"id":"feature-flags-and-configuration","text":"Feature Flags and Configuration","level":3},{"id":"type-safety","text":"Type Safety","level":2},{"id":"typescript-declarations","text":"TypeScript Declarations","level":3},{"id":"runtime-validation","text":"Runtime Validation","level":3},{"id":"security-best-practices","text":"Security Best Practices","level":2},{"id":"1-never-expose-secrets-to-client","text":"1. Never Expose Secrets to Client","level":3},{"id":"2-use-appropriate-prefixes","text":"2. Use Appropriate Prefixes","level":3},{"id":"3-validate-required-variables","text":"3. Validate Required Variables","level":3},{"id":"production-checklist","text":"Production Checklist","level":2},{"id":"common-problems","text":"Common Problems","level":2},{"id":"environment-variable-is-undefined","text":"Environment Variable is Undefined","level":3},{"id":"runtime-client-environment-variables-in-production","text":"Runtime Client Environment Variables in Production","level":3},{"id":"variable-not-updating","text":"Variable Not Updating","level":3},{"id":"typescript-errors","text":"TypeScript Errors","level":3},{"id":"security-secret-exposed-to-client","text":"Security: Secret Exposed to Client","level":3},{"id":"build-errors-in-production","text":"Build Errors in Production","level":3},{"id":"server-build-configuration","text":"Server Build Configuration","level":2},{"id":"static-node-env-replacement","text":"Static NODE_ENV Replacement","level":3},{"id":"configuring-static-replacement","text":"Configuring Static Replacement","level":3},{"id":"when-to-disable-static-replacement","text":"When to Disable Static Replacement","level":3},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLearn how to securely configure and use environment variables in your TanStack Start application across different contexts (server functions, client code, and build processes).\n\n> **Read env per-request, not at module scope.** On Cloudflare Workers and other edge SSR runtimes, env vars are injected at request time — module-level `process.env.X` reads run before the env exists and evaluate to `undefined` even on the server. Always read `process.env` inside `.handler()`, middleware `.server()`, server-route handlers, or other per-request callbacks. Reading at module scope also risks inlining secrets into the client bundle. (On Cloudflare Workers specifically, the canonical way to read env from anywhere — including module scope — is the [`cloudflare:workers` env binding](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/environment-variables/).)\n\n## Quick Start\n\nTanStack Start automatically loads `.env` files and makes variables available in both server and client contexts with proper security boundaries. Server code can read unprefixed variables from `process.env`; client code can only read variables exposed by your build tool's public prefix.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```bash\n# .env\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb\nVITE_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Server function - can access any environment variable\nconst getUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const db = await connect(process.env.DATABASE_URL) // ✅ Server-only\n  return db.user.findFirst()\n})\n\n// Client component - only VITE_ prefixed variables\nexport function AppHeader() {\n  return <h1>{import.meta.env.VITE_APP_NAME}</h1> // ✅ Client-safe\n}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```bash\n# .env\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Server function - can access any environment variable\nconst getUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const db = await connect(process.env.DATABASE_URL) // ✅ Server-only\n  return db.user.findFirst()\n})\n\n// Client component - only PUBLIC_ prefixed variables by default\nexport function AppHeader() {\n  return <h1>{import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APP_NAME}</h1> // ✅ Client-safe\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Environment Variable Contexts\n\n### Server-Side Context (Server Functions & API Routes)\n\nServer functions can access **any** environment variable using `process.env`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\n// Database connection (server-only)\nconst connectToDatabase = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const connectionString = process.env.DATABASE_URL // No prefix needed\n  const apiKey = process.env.EXTERNAL_API_SECRET // Stays on server\n\n  // These variables are never exposed to the client\n  return await database.connect(connectionString)\n})\n\n// Authentication (server-only)\nconst authenticateUser = createServerFn()\n  .validator(z.object({ token: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const jwtSecret = process.env.JWT_SECRET // Server-only\n    return jwt.verify(data.token, jwtSecret)\n  })\n```\n\n### Client-Side Context (Components & Client Code)\n\nClient code can only access variables with your build tool's public prefix.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\nVite exposes variables with the `VITE_` prefix:\n\n```typescript\n// Client configuration\nexport function ApiProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL     // ✅ Public\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_KEY  // ✅ Public\n\n  // This would be undefined (security feature):\n  // const secret = import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL   // ❌ Undefined\n\n  return (\n    <ApiContext.Provider value={{ apiUrl, apiKey }}>\n      {children}\n    </ApiContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\n// Feature flags\nexport function FeatureGatedComponent() {\n  const enableNewFeature = import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_FEATURE === 'true'\n\n  if (!enableNewFeature) return null\n\n  return <NewFeature />\n}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\nRsbuild exposes variables with the `PUBLIC_` prefix by default:\n\n```typescript\n// Client configuration\nexport function ApiProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL // ✅ Public\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_KEY // ✅ Public\n\n  // This would be undefined (security feature):\n  // const secret = import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL // ❌ Undefined\n\n  return (\n    <ApiContext.Provider value={{ apiUrl, apiKey }}>\n      {children}\n    </ApiContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\n// Feature flags\nexport function FeatureGatedComponent() {\n  const enableNewFeature = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ENABLE_NEW_FEATURE === 'true'\n\n  if (!enableNewFeature) return null\n\n  return <NewFeature />\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Environment File Setup\n\n### File Hierarchy (Loaded in Order)\n\nTanStack Start automatically loads environment files in this order:\n\n```\n.env.local          # Local overrides (add to .gitignore)\n.env.production     # Production-specific variables\n.env.development    # Development-specific variables\n.env                # Default variables (commit to git)\n```\n\n### Example Setup\n\n**.env** (committed to repository):\n\n```bash\n# Public configuration (Vite uses VITE_; Rsbuild uses PUBLIC_ by default)\nVITE_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\n\n# Server configuration templates\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/myapp_dev\nREDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379\n```\n\n**.env.local** (add to .gitignore):\n\n```bash\n# Override for local development\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/myapp_local\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\nJWT_SECRET=your-local-secret\n```\n\n**.env.production**:\n\n```bash\n# Production overrides\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.myapp.com\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.myapp.com\nDATABASE_POOL_SIZE=20\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Database Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/database.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst getDatabaseConnection = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const config = {\n    url: process.env.DATABASE_URL,\n    maxConnections: parseInt(process.env.DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS || '10'),\n    ssl: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',\n  }\n\n  return createConnection(config)\n})\n```\n\n### Authentication Provider Setup\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/auth.ts (Server)\nexport const authConfig = {\n  secret: process.env.AUTH_SECRET,\n  providers: {\n    auth0: {\n      domain: process.env.AUTH0_DOMAIN,\n      clientId: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n      clientSecret: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET, // Server-only\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// src/components/AuthProvider.tsx (Client)\nexport function AuthProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <Auth0Provider\n      domain={import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN}\n      clientId={import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID}\n      // No client secret here - it stays on the server\n    >\n      {children}\n    </Auth0Provider>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### External API Integration\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/external-api.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\n// Server-side API calls (can use secret keys)\nconst fetchUserData = createServerFn()\n  .validator(z.object({ userId: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(\n      `${process.env.EXTERNAL_API_URL}/users/${data.userId}`,\n      {\n        headers: {\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.EXTERNAL_API_SECRET}`,\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n        },\n      },\n    )\n\n    return response.json()\n  })\n\n// Client-side API calls (public endpoints only)\nexport function usePublicData() {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL\n\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['public-data'],\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`${apiUrl}/public/stats`).then((r) => r.json()),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Feature Flags and Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/features.ts\nexport const featureFlags = {\n  enableNewDashboard: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD === 'true',\n  enableAnalytics: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS === 'true',\n  debugMode: import.meta.env.VITE_DEBUG_MODE === 'true',\n}\n\n// Usage in components\nexport function Dashboard() {\n  if (featureFlags.enableNewDashboard) {\n    return <NewDashboard />\n  }\n\n  return <LegacyDashboard />\n}\n```\n\n## Type Safety\n\n### TypeScript Declarations\n\nCreate `src/env.d.ts` to add type safety:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```typescript\n/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // Client-side environment variables\n  readonly VITE_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly VITE_API_URL: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n  readonly VITE_SENTRY_DSN?: string\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD?: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n\n// Server-side environment variables\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      readonly DATABASE_URL: string\n      readonly REDIS_URL: string\n      readonly JWT_SECRET: string\n      readonly AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET: string\n      readonly STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: string\n      readonly NODE_ENV: 'development' | 'production' | 'test'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```typescript\n/// <reference types=\"@rsbuild/core/types\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // Client-side environment variables\n  readonly PUBLIC_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_API_URL: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN?: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD?: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n\n// Server-side environment variables\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      readonly DATABASE_URL: string\n      readonly REDIS_URL: string\n      readonly JWT_SECRET: string\n      readonly AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET: string\n      readonly STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: string\n      readonly NODE_ENV: 'development' | 'production' | 'test'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### Runtime Validation\n\nUse Zod for runtime validation of environment variables:\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/env.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  DATABASE_URL: z.url(),\n  JWT_SECRET: z.string().min(32),\n  NODE_ENV: z.enum(['development', 'production', 'test']),\n})\n\nconst clientEnvSchema = z.object({\n  VITE_APP_NAME: z.string(),\n  VITE_API_URL: z.url(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: z.string(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: z.string(),\n})\n\n// Validate server environment\n// NOTE: Module-level parse runs at module load. Fine for Node.js;\n// on Cloudflare Workers (and other edge runtimes) `process.env` is\n// empty at module load, so wrap this in a function and call it\n// inside `.handler()` instead:\n//\n//   export const getServerEnv = () => envSchema.parse(process.env)\n//\n// Then read `getServerEnv()` per-request from server functions/middleware.\nexport const serverEnv = envSchema.parse(process.env)\n\n// Validate client environment (build-time, always safe)\nexport const clientEnv = clientEnvSchema.parse(import.meta.env)\n```\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### 1. Never Expose Secrets to Client\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Secret exposed to client bundle\nconst config = {\n  apiKey: import.meta.env.VITE_SECRET_API_KEY, // This will be in your JS bundle!\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Keep secrets on server\nconst getApiData = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\n    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.SECRET_API_KEY}` },\n  })\n  return response.json()\n})\n```\n\n### 2. Use Appropriate Prefixes\n\n```bash\n# ✅ Server-only (no prefix)\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://...\nJWT_SECRET=super-secret-key\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...\n\n# ✅ Client-safe (Vite uses VITE_; Rsbuild uses PUBLIC_ by default)\nVITE_APP_NAME=My App\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My App\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\n```\n\n### 3. Validate Required Variables\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/validation.ts\nconst requiredServerEnv = ['DATABASE_URL', 'JWT_SECRET'] as const\n\nconst requiredClientEnv = ['VITE_APP_NAME', 'VITE_API_URL'] as const // Use PUBLIC_ names for Rsbuild\n\n// Validate on server startup\nfor (const key of requiredServerEnv) {\n  if (!process.env[key]) {\n    throw new Error(`Missing required environment variable: ${key}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// Validate client environment at build time\nfor (const key of requiredClientEnv) {\n  if (!import.meta.env[key]) {\n    throw new Error(`Missing required environment variable: ${key}`)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] All sensitive variables are server-only (no `VITE_` or `PUBLIC_` prefix)\n- [ ] Client variables use your build tool's public prefix (`VITE_` for Vite, `PUBLIC_` for Rsbuild)\n- [ ] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore`\n- [ ] Production environment variables are configured on hosting platform\n- [ ] Required environment variables are validated at startup\n- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in source code\n- [ ] Database URLs use connection pooling in production\n- [ ] API keys are rotated regularly\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Environment Variable is Undefined\n\n**Problem**: `import.meta.env.MY_VARIABLE` returns `undefined`\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Add correct prefix**: Use your build tool's public prefix (e.g. `VITE_MY_VARIABLE` for Vite or `PUBLIC_MY_VARIABLE` for Rsbuild)\n2. **Restart development server** after adding new variables\n3. **Check file location**: `.env` file must be in project root\n4. **Verify build tool configuration**: Ensure variables are properly injected\n\n**Example**:\n\n```bash\n# ❌ Won't work in client code\nAPI_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works in client code\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ❌ Won't bundle the variable (assuming it is not set in the environment of the build)\nnpm run build\n\n# ✅ Works in client code and will bundle the variable for production\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n```\n\n### Runtime Client Environment Variables in Production\n\n**Problem**: If public client variables are replaced at bundle time only, how to make runtime variables available on the client?\n\n**Solutions**:\n\nPass variables from the server down to the client:\n\n```tsx\nconst getRuntimeVar = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(() => {\n  return process.env.MY_RUNTIME_VAR // notice `process.env` on the server, and no public prefix\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const foo = await getRuntimeVar()\n    return { foo }\n  },\n  component: RouteComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  const { foo } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  // ... use your variable however you want\n}\n```\n\n### Variable Not Updating\n\n**Problem**: Environment variable changes aren't reflected\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. Restart development server\n2. Check if you're modifying the correct `.env` file\n3. Verify file hierarchy (`.env.local` overrides `.env`)\n\n### TypeScript Errors\n\n**Problem**: `Property 'VITE_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'` or `Property 'PUBLIC_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'`\n\n**Solution**: Add to `src/env.d.ts`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  readonly VITE_MY_VAR: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_MY_VAR: string\n}\n```\n\n### Security: Secret Exposed to Client\n\n**Problem**: Sensitive data appearing in client bundle\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. Remove `VITE_` or `PUBLIC_` prefix from sensitive variables\n2. Move sensitive operations to server functions\n3. Use build tools to verify no secrets in client bundle\n\n### Build Errors in Production\n\n**Problem**: Missing environment variables in production build\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. Configure variables on hosting platform\n2. Validate required variables at build time\n3. Use deployment-specific `.env` files\n\n## Server Build Configuration\n\n### Static `NODE_ENV` Replacement\n\nBy default, TanStack Start statically replaces `process.env.NODE_ENV` in **server builds** at build time. This enables dead code elimination (tree-shaking) for development-only code paths in your server bundle.\n\n**Why this matters:** Vite automatically replaces `process.env.NODE_ENV` in client builds, but server builds run in Node.js where `process.env` is a real runtime object. Without static replacement, code like this would remain in your production server bundle:\n\n```typescript\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {\n  // This code would NOT be eliminated without static replacement\n  enableDevTools()\n  logDebugInfo()\n}\n```\n\nWith static replacement enabled (the default), the build tool sees `\"production\" === 'development'` and eliminates the entire block.\n\n### Configuring Static Replacement\n\nThe replacement is controlled by the `server.build.staticNodeEnv` option:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport viteReact from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      server: {\n        build: {\n          // Replace process.env.NODE_ENV at build time (default: true)\n          staticNodeEnv: true,\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n    viteReact(),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      server: {\n        build: {\n          // Replace process.env.NODE_ENV at build time (default: true)\n          staticNodeEnv: true,\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe replacement value is determined in this order:\n\n1. `process.env.NODE_ENV` at build time (if set)\n2. The build tool's `mode` (e.g., from `--mode staging`)\n3. `\"production\"` (fallback)\n\n### When to Disable Static Replacement\n\nSet `staticNodeEnv: false` if you need `NODE_ENV` to remain dynamic at runtime:\n\n```ts\ntanstackStart({\n  server: {\n    build: {\n      staticNodeEnv: false, // Keep NODE_ENV dynamic at runtime\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nCommon reasons to disable:\n\n- **Same build, multiple environments**: Deploying one build artifact to staging and production\n- **Runtime environment detection**: Code that must check the actual runtime environment\n- **Testing production builds locally**: Running production builds with `NODE_ENV=development`\n\n> **Note:** Disabling static replacement means development-only code paths will remain in your production bundle and be evaluated at runtime.\n\n> **Important:** If you disable `staticNodeEnv`, you **must** set `NODE_ENV=production` at runtime when running your server in production. Without this, React (and possibly other libraries) will run in development mode, which is significantly slower and includes extra warnings and checks not intended for production use.\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [Code Execution Patterns](./code-execution-patterns.md) - Learn about server vs client code execution\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) - Learn more about server-side code\n- [Hosting](./hosting.md) - Platform-specific environment variable configuration\n- [Vite Environment Variables](https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) - Official Vite documentation\n- [Rsbuild Environment Variables](https://rsbuild.dev/guide/advanced/env-vars) - Official Rsbuild documentation\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: environment-variables\ntitle: Environment Variables\n---\n\nLearn how to securely configure and use environment variables in your TanStack Start application across different contexts (server functions, client code, and build processes).\n\n> **Read env per-request, not at module scope.** On Cloudflare Workers and other edge SSR runtimes, env vars are injected at request time — module-level `process.env.X` reads run before the env exists and evaluate to `undefined` even on the server. Always read `process.env` inside `.handler()`, middleware `.server()`, server-route handlers, or other per-request callbacks. Reading at module scope also risks inlining secrets into the client bundle. (On Cloudflare Workers specifically, the canonical way to read env from anywhere — including module scope — is the [`cloudflare:workers` env binding](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/environment-variables/).)\n\n## Quick Start\n\nTanStack Start automatically loads `.env` files and makes variables available in both server and client contexts with proper security boundaries. Server code can read unprefixed variables from `process.env`; client code can only read variables exposed by your build tool's public prefix.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```bash\n# .env\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb\nVITE_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Server function - can access any environment variable\nconst getUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const db = await connect(process.env.DATABASE_URL) // ✅ Server-only\n  return db.user.findFirst()\n})\n\n// Client component - only VITE_ prefixed variables\nexport function AppHeader() {\n  return <h1>{import.meta.env.VITE_APP_NAME}</h1> // ✅ Client-safe\n}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```bash\n# .env\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Server function - can access any environment variable\nconst getUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const db = await connect(process.env.DATABASE_URL) // ✅ Server-only\n  return db.user.findFirst()\n})\n\n// Client component - only PUBLIC_ prefixed variables by default\nexport function AppHeader() {\n  return <h1>{import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APP_NAME}</h1> // ✅ Client-safe\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Environment Variable Contexts\n\n### Server-Side Context (Server Functions & API Routes)\n\nServer functions can access **any** environment variable using `process.env`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\n// Database connection (server-only)\nconst connectToDatabase = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const connectionString = process.env.DATABASE_URL // No prefix needed\n  const apiKey = process.env.EXTERNAL_API_SECRET // Stays on server\n\n  // These variables are never exposed to the client\n  return await database.connect(connectionString)\n})\n\n// Authentication (server-only)\nconst authenticateUser = createServerFn()\n  .validator(z.object({ token: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const jwtSecret = process.env.JWT_SECRET // Server-only\n    return jwt.verify(data.token, jwtSecret)\n  })\n```\n\n### Client-Side Context (Components & Client Code)\n\nClient code can only access variables with your build tool's public prefix.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\nVite exposes variables with the `VITE_` prefix:\n\n```typescript\n// Client configuration\nexport function ApiProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL     // ✅ Public\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_KEY  // ✅ Public\n\n  // This would be undefined (security feature):\n  // const secret = import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL   // ❌ Undefined\n\n  return (\n    <ApiContext.Provider value={{ apiUrl, apiKey }}>\n      {children}\n    </ApiContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\n// Feature flags\nexport function FeatureGatedComponent() {\n  const enableNewFeature = import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_FEATURE === 'true'\n\n  if (!enableNewFeature) return null\n\n  return <NewFeature />\n}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\nRsbuild exposes variables with the `PUBLIC_` prefix by default:\n\n```typescript\n// Client configuration\nexport function ApiProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL // ✅ Public\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_KEY // ✅ Public\n\n  // This would be undefined (security feature):\n  // const secret = import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL // ❌ Undefined\n\n  return (\n    <ApiContext.Provider value={{ apiUrl, apiKey }}>\n      {children}\n    </ApiContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\n// Feature flags\nexport function FeatureGatedComponent() {\n  const enableNewFeature = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ENABLE_NEW_FEATURE === 'true'\n\n  if (!enableNewFeature) return null\n\n  return <NewFeature />\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Environment File Setup\n\n### File Hierarchy (Loaded in Order)\n\nTanStack Start automatically loads environment files in this order:\n\n```\n.env.local          # Local overrides (add to .gitignore)\n.env.production     # Production-specific variables\n.env.development    # Development-specific variables\n.env                # Default variables (commit to git)\n```\n\n### Example Setup\n\n**.env** (committed to repository):\n\n```bash\n# Public configuration (Vite uses VITE_; Rsbuild uses PUBLIC_ by default)\nVITE_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My TanStack Start App\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\n\n# Server configuration templates\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/myapp_dev\nREDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379\n```\n\n**.env.local** (add to .gitignore):\n\n```bash\n# Override for local development\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/myapp_local\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\nJWT_SECRET=your-local-secret\n```\n\n**.env.production**:\n\n```bash\n# Production overrides\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.myapp.com\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.myapp.com\nDATABASE_POOL_SIZE=20\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Database Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/database.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst getDatabaseConnection = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const config = {\n    url: process.env.DATABASE_URL,\n    maxConnections: parseInt(process.env.DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS || '10'),\n    ssl: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',\n  }\n\n  return createConnection(config)\n})\n```\n\n### Authentication Provider Setup\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/auth.ts (Server)\nexport const authConfig = {\n  secret: process.env.AUTH_SECRET,\n  providers: {\n    auth0: {\n      domain: process.env.AUTH0_DOMAIN,\n      clientId: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n      clientSecret: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET, // Server-only\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// src/components/AuthProvider.tsx (Client)\nexport function AuthProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <Auth0Provider\n      domain={import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN}\n      clientId={import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID}\n      // No client secret here - it stays on the server\n    >\n      {children}\n    </Auth0Provider>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### External API Integration\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/external-api.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\n// Server-side API calls (can use secret keys)\nconst fetchUserData = createServerFn()\n  .validator(z.object({ userId: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(\n      `${process.env.EXTERNAL_API_URL}/users/${data.userId}`,\n      {\n        headers: {\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.EXTERNAL_API_SECRET}`,\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n        },\n      },\n    )\n\n    return response.json()\n  })\n\n// Client-side API calls (public endpoints only)\nexport function usePublicData() {\n  const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL\n\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['public-data'],\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`${apiUrl}/public/stats`).then((r) => r.json()),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Feature Flags and Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/features.ts\nexport const featureFlags = {\n  enableNewDashboard: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD === 'true',\n  enableAnalytics: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS === 'true',\n  debugMode: import.meta.env.VITE_DEBUG_MODE === 'true',\n}\n\n// Usage in components\nexport function Dashboard() {\n  if (featureFlags.enableNewDashboard) {\n    return <NewDashboard />\n  }\n\n  return <LegacyDashboard />\n}\n```\n\n## Type Safety\n\n### TypeScript Declarations\n\nCreate `src/env.d.ts` to add type safety:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```typescript\n/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // Client-side environment variables\n  readonly VITE_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly VITE_API_URL: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n  readonly VITE_SENTRY_DSN?: string\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD?: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n\n// Server-side environment variables\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      readonly DATABASE_URL: string\n      readonly REDIS_URL: string\n      readonly JWT_SECRET: string\n      readonly AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET: string\n      readonly STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: string\n      readonly NODE_ENV: 'development' | 'production' | 'test'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```typescript\n/// <reference types=\"@rsbuild/core/types\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // Client-side environment variables\n  readonly PUBLIC_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_API_URL: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN?: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD?: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n\n// Server-side environment variables\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      readonly DATABASE_URL: string\n      readonly REDIS_URL: string\n      readonly JWT_SECRET: string\n      readonly AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET: string\n      readonly STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: string\n      readonly NODE_ENV: 'development' | 'production' | 'test'\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### Runtime Validation\n\nUse Zod for runtime validation of environment variables:\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/env.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  DATABASE_URL: z.url(),\n  JWT_SECRET: z.string().min(32),\n  NODE_ENV: z.enum(['development', 'production', 'test']),\n})\n\nconst clientEnvSchema = z.object({\n  VITE_APP_NAME: z.string(),\n  VITE_API_URL: z.url(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: z.string(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: z.string(),\n})\n\n// Validate server environment\n// NOTE: Module-level parse runs at module load. Fine for Node.js;\n// on Cloudflare Workers (and other edge runtimes) `process.env` is\n// empty at module load, so wrap this in a function and call it\n// inside `.handler()` instead:\n//\n//   export const getServerEnv = () => envSchema.parse(process.env)\n//\n// Then read `getServerEnv()` per-request from server functions/middleware.\nexport const serverEnv = envSchema.parse(process.env)\n\n// Validate client environment (build-time, always safe)\nexport const clientEnv = clientEnvSchema.parse(import.meta.env)\n```\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### 1. Never Expose Secrets to Client\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Secret exposed to client bundle\nconst config = {\n  apiKey: import.meta.env.VITE_SECRET_API_KEY, // This will be in your JS bundle!\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Keep secrets on server\nconst getApiData = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\n    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.SECRET_API_KEY}` },\n  })\n  return response.json()\n})\n```\n\n### 2. Use Appropriate Prefixes\n\n```bash\n# ✅ Server-only (no prefix)\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://...\nJWT_SECRET=super-secret-key\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...\n\n# ✅ Client-safe (Vite uses VITE_; Rsbuild uses PUBLIC_ by default)\nVITE_APP_NAME=My App\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\nPUBLIC_APP_NAME=My App\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...\n```\n\n### 3. Validate Required Variables\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/validation.ts\nconst requiredServerEnv = ['DATABASE_URL', 'JWT_SECRET'] as const\n\nconst requiredClientEnv = ['VITE_APP_NAME', 'VITE_API_URL'] as const // Use PUBLIC_ names for Rsbuild\n\n// Validate on server startup\nfor (const key of requiredServerEnv) {\n  if (!process.env[key]) {\n    throw new Error(`Missing required environment variable: ${key}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// Validate client environment at build time\nfor (const key of requiredClientEnv) {\n  if (!import.meta.env[key]) {\n    throw new Error(`Missing required environment variable: ${key}`)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] All sensitive variables are server-only (no `VITE_` or `PUBLIC_` prefix)\n- [ ] Client variables use your build tool's public prefix (`VITE_` for Vite, `PUBLIC_` for Rsbuild)\n- [ ] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore`\n- [ ] Production environment variables are configured on hosting platform\n- [ ] Required environment variables are validated at startup\n- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in source code\n- [ ] Database URLs use connection pooling in production\n- [ ] API keys are rotated regularly\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Environment Variable is Undefined\n\n**Problem**: `import.meta.env.MY_VARIABLE` returns `undefined`\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Add correct prefix**: Use your build tool's public prefix (e.g. `VITE_MY_VARIABLE` for Vite or `PUBLIC_MY_VARIABLE` for Rsbuild)\n2. **Restart development server** after adding new variables\n3. **Check file location**: `.env` file must be in project root\n4. **Verify build tool configuration**: Ensure variables are properly injected\n\n**Example**:\n\n```bash\n# ❌ Won't work in client code\nAPI_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works in client code\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ❌ Won't bundle the variable (assuming it is not set in the environment of the build)\nnpm run build\n\n# ✅ Works in client code and will bundle the variable for production\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n```\n\n### Runtime Client Environment Variables in Production\n\n**Problem**: If public client variables are replaced at bundle time only, how to make runtime variables available on the client?\n\n**Solutions**:\n\nPass variables from the server down to the client:\n\n```tsx\nconst getRuntimeVar = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(() => {\n  return process.env.MY_RUNTIME_VAR // notice `process.env` on the server, and no public prefix\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const foo = await getRuntimeVar()\n    return { foo }\n  },\n  component: RouteComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  const { foo } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  // ... use your variable however you want\n}\n```\n\n### Variable Not Updating\n\n**Problem**: Environment variable changes aren't reflected\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. Restart development server\n2. Check if you're modifying the correct `.env` file\n3. Verify file hierarchy (`.env.local` overrides `.env`)\n\n### TypeScript Errors\n\n**Problem**: `Property 'VITE_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'` or `Property 'PUBLIC_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'`\n\n**Solution**: Add to `src/env.d.ts`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  readonly VITE_MY_VAR: string\n  readonly PUBLIC_MY_VAR: string\n}\n```\n\n### Security: Secret Exposed to Client\n\n**Problem**: Sensitive data appearing in client bundle\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. Remove `VITE_` or `PUBLIC_` prefix from sensitive variables\n2. Move sensitive operations to server functions\n3. Use build tools to verify no secrets in client bundle\n\n### Build Errors in Production\n\n**Problem**: Missing environment variables in production build\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. Configure variables on hosting platform\n2. Validate required variables at build time\n3. Use deployment-specific `.env` files\n\n## Server Build Configuration\n\n### Static `NODE_ENV` Replacement\n\nBy default, TanStack Start statically replaces `process.env.NODE_ENV` in **server builds** at build time. This enables dead code elimination (tree-shaking) for development-only code paths in your server bundle.\n\n**Why this matters:** Vite automatically replaces `process.env.NODE_ENV` in client builds, but server builds run in Node.js where `process.env` is a real runtime object. Without static replacement, code like this would remain in your production server bundle:\n\n```typescript\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {\n  // This code would NOT be eliminated without static replacement\n  enableDevTools()\n  logDebugInfo()\n}\n```\n\nWith static replacement enabled (the default), the build tool sees `\"production\" === 'development'` and eliminates the entire block.\n\n### Configuring Static Replacement\n\nThe replacement is controlled by the `server.build.staticNodeEnv` option:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport viteReact from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      server: {\n        build: {\n          // Replace process.env.NODE_ENV at build time (default: true)\n          staticNodeEnv: true,\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n    viteReact(),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      server: {\n        build: {\n          // Replace process.env.NODE_ENV at build time (default: true)\n          staticNodeEnv: true,\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe replacement value is determined in this order:\n\n1. `process.env.NODE_ENV` at build time (if set)\n2. The build tool's `mode` (e.g., from `--mode staging`)\n3. `\"production\"` (fallback)\n\n### When to Disable Static Replacement\n\nSet `staticNodeEnv: false` if you need `NODE_ENV` to remain dynamic at runtime:\n\n```ts\ntanstackStart({\n  server: {\n    build: {\n      staticNodeEnv: false, // Keep NODE_ENV dynamic at runtime\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nCommon reasons to disable:\n\n- **Same build, multiple environments**: Deploying one build artifact to staging and production\n- **Runtime environment detection**: Code that must check the actual runtime environment\n- **Testing production builds locally**: Running production builds with `NODE_ENV=development`\n\n> **Note:** Disabling static replacement means development-only code paths will remain in your production bundle and be evaluated at runtime.\n\n> **Important:** If you disable `staticNodeEnv`, you **must** set `NODE_ENV=production` at runtime when running your server in production. Without this, React (and possibly other libraries) will run in development mode, which is significantly slower and includes extra warnings and checks not intended for production use.\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [Code Execution Patterns](./code-execution-patterns.md) - Learn about server vs client code execution\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) - Learn more about server-side code\n- [Hosting](./hosting.md) - Platform-specific environment variable configuration\n- [Vite Environment Variables](https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) - Official Vite documentation\n- [Rsbuild Environment Variables](https://rsbuild.dev/guide/advanced/env-vars) - Official Rsbuild documentation\n"}
